{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":303960,"num_turns":27,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"de495939-000e-4e7f-ada6-dc861ba8da70","total_cost_usd":0.8153468,"usage":{"input_tokens":24,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101455,"cache_read_input_tokens":650394,"output_tokens":27705,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":11312},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":101455,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7383,"cache_read_input_tokens":88002,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13453,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13453},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":2285,"outputTokens":13,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00235,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":24,"outputTokens":27705,"cacheReadInputTokens":650394,"cacheCreationInputTokens":101455,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8129968,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"architecture_summary\":\"The target design is sound in skeleton: a deterministic local authority (persistent task-contract graph, Git-committed evidence records, hash-bound GDD conformance derivation) owns 'what is true', while bounded LLM workers (currently Claude and OpenAI/Codex behind a shared AgentRuntime transport) act as replaceable, evidence-gated implementers with human merge/approval as the final gate. Schema-v2 task contracts correctly separate approved definition from mutable completion claims, and Phase 3's evidence-derived conformance state machine correctly ties completion to committed Git/GDD-hash facts rather than self-reported status. However, three consecutive implementation stages since Milestone 1 (Phase 1-3 state correction, then Stage 3-4A-4D AgentRuntime/provider-adapter work) have been spent entirely on process/meta-infrastructure. The concrete deliverable of all Stage 4 work is that ArchitectureReview -- a tool that reviews the pipeline itself -- now runs through a fully generalized, dual-provider (Claude + Codex), fail-closed transport layer with capability mapping, budget translation, and trust-boundary hardening. No provider adapter supports repository_write; TaskExecutionRunner is an untested 39-line wrapper never exercised on a real task; and the one demonstrated repair loop that actually shipped a working feature (Assignment 6 GER with runtime-feedback repair and no-op detection) has not been ported to the new AgentRuntime/TaskExecution stack at all. Meanwhile NSC-003, the team's own designated 'strong anchor' ready task, sits untouched, and CURRENT_STATE.md itself now says it needs further human design resolution before dispatch. The architecture's philosophy is correct; its recent build sequencing has repeatedly violated the project's own stated rule (ADR-019) that infrastructure must be exercised on real gameplay work rather than becoming a self-perpetuating side project.\",\"overall_verdict\":\"partially_unsound\",\"verdict_reason\":\"The state/authority model (task-contract schema 2.0, immutable evidence records, Git/GDD-hash-bound conformance derivation) is genuinely sound and should be kept. But the architecture as currently sequenced is not fit for its stated purpose of accelerating real development, because (1) the newest and most expensive layer of work -- a dual-provider AgentRuntime with full capability-mapping/fail-closed enforcement -- has zero write capability and its only live consumer is a recursive self-review tool, not game code; (2) the one proven quality mechanism (GER with runtime-evidence repair and no-op detection) that actually converted a failing implementation into a working feature is orphaned outside the new runtime; (3) there is no automated linkage between GDD edits and the 37 task contracts that embed literal quoted GDD text, which is a real gap given the explicit iterative-GDD requirement. These are not merely stylistic overbuilding; they mean the pipeline, as built, cannot currently deliver a single unit of validated gameplay work end to end, three days after the milestone checkpoint that was supposed to trigger exactly that kind of proof.\",\"strong_decisions\":[\"Task-contract schema 2.0 correctly separates approved definition (Tasks/*.yaml) from mutable completion truth, closing a real self-reported-completion risk.\",\"Phase 3 evidence-derived conformance binds completion to committed Git commit/tree, canonical GDD hash, and evidence-artifact blob SHAs read only from HEAD, so a dirty working tree or uncommitted evidence cannot fake conformance -- verified directly (NSC-023 flipped not_delivered -> conformant only after evidence was committed).\",\"GDD-hash binding in evidence records correctly treats a GDD edit as invalidating existing conformance (needs_revalidation) rather than assuming a one-time-correct bootstrap; this is the right per-task mechanism for a moving design target.\",\"ADR-015/ADR-016 (runtime evidence as first-class validation input; no-op refinement counted as failed progress) are real lessons from an actual failure (the Assignment 6 camera) and were correctly generalized as durable project rules.\",\"Deterministic scene builder + EditMode/PlayMode test pattern (DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder + CommittedSceneCameraConformanceTests) keeps Unity scene state reproducible and testable rather than hand-edited, which is good practice this project actually uses.\",\"Restraint on supervisor, worktrees, GitHub dashboard, continuous autonomy, and parallel workers -- these remain correctly unimplemented rather than spawned speculatively, showing the team can defer some things well.\",\"Fail-closed defaults for unsupported capabilities, non-null token_limit, and repository_write are conservative and appropriate for a trusted single-developer project that has not yet earned autonomous write trust.\"],\"structural_flaws\":[\"No provider adapter (Claude or Codex) supports repository_write or approved_command_execution; the entire Stage 4 investment therefore cannot commit a single line of game code today.\",\"The one proven repair/quality loop (Assignment 6 GER: evaluate -> runtime feedback -> refine -> circuit breaker) has not been integrated into AgentRuntime/TaskExecution at all; if write capability were added tomorrow, the new pipeline would ship code with less quality gating than the prototype that already worked.\",\"Task contracts embed literal quoted GDD text as gdd_evidence/acceptance criteria across 37 files with no automated mechanism to detect when a GDD edit has invalidated those embedded quotes short of a full, expensive, human-gated reconciliation run.\",\"AgentInvocationRequest/TaskExecutionRequest separation (ADR-039) is architecturally defensible but was built for multiple hypothetical consumers (ExecutionCrew, Reconciliation) when it currently has exactly one real consumer (ArchitectureReview) that does not even need task identity -- premature generalization ahead of proven need.\",\"Repository-capable context_paths are described as 'prompt guidance rather than a hardened sandbox boundary' -- the read containment is soft/trust-based, acceptable for a single trusted developer but inconsistent with the otherwise heavy fail-closed posture applied elsewhere.\"],\"observed_failure_solutions\":[\"Static-pass-but-runtime-broken camera (Assignment 6) -> runtime evidence made first-class validation input (ADR-015), proven to work.\",\"Refiner claiming 'implemented' with no file changes (Assignment 6 Pass 3) -> no-op refinement now counts as failed repair against the circuit-breaker budget (ADR-016), proven to work.\",\"Mutable task status files could self-declare completion without evidence -> task-contract schema 2.0 plus Phase 3 evidence-derived conformance removed status as an authority field and requires committed Git/GDD-hash-bound proof.\"],\"hypothetical_failure_solutions\":[\"Full dual-provider (Claude + Codex) capability-mapping, budget-translation, and fail-closed enforcement layer -- built for a provider swap or comparison that has never happened and is explicitly deferred future work.\",\"Adversarial provider trust-boundary hardening (malformed/cyclic JSON, polymorphic mutable values, malicious provider output) in AgentRuntime -- defends against an adversarial model operator in a project ADR-038 itself frames as a trusted single-user boundary.\",\"Multi-model independent verification crew for reconciliation bootstrap (2+ Claude models auditing coverage) -- used once successfully, but kept as standing infrastructure for 'later substantial reconciliation events' that have not recurred.\",\"Generalized AgentInvocationRequest/TaskExecutionRequest layering above AgentRuntime to support future ExecutionCrew and Reconciliation consumers that do not yet exist.\"],\"overengineering\":[\"Running the full 8-reviewer + synthesis + adversarial-critique ArchitectureReview process through two independently engineered providers before either provider can write a single file is disproportionate to any near-term decision it enables.\",\"Building generic, schema-validated, budget-enforced AgentRuntime capability plumbing (repository_read/search/write, approved_command_execution, token_limit, turn_limit translation) primarily to serve a self-review tool rather than the one real pending gameplay ticket.\",\"Maintaining and documenting a standing multi-model verification-crew capability for reconciliation bootstrap when only one bootstrap event has ever required it.\"],\"missing_components\":[\"Any working write-capable execution path from AgentRuntime/TaskExecution through to a Git commit -- currently the single biggest gap for delivering any real feature.\",\"A GER-equivalent evaluate/refine/circuit-breaker loop wired into the new AgentRuntime/TaskExecution stack (currently only exists, disconnected, in the Assignment 6 prototype).\",\"A scoped GDD-change-impact mechanism that maps an edited GDD passage to the specific task contracts whose acceptance criteria/gdd_evidence quote it, short of full reconciliation.\",\"Any implementation of the supervisor, branch/worktree/Draft-PR automation, RAG-backed compact context builder, Progressive Decomposer, or Artifact Authority Gate -- all remain design documents only, which is fine as long as they are not built before the write-capable single-ticket loop is proven.\"],\"state_and_authority_concerns\":[\"Necessary and currently correct: task-contract definition vs. immutable evidence record vs. derived current-conformance state are three distinct, non-overlapping authorities, each committed to Git, with no single source claiming to 'be' completion truth.\",\"Necessary and currently correct: readiness/dispatch authorization is explicitly and verifiably denied (taskcontrol ready/authorize both fail closed), so no accidental autonomous execution can occur.\",\"Duplicative/premature: the AgentInvocationRequest vs. TaskExecutionRequest split exists mainly to protect a provider-neutral layer from a task-execution consumer that has not yet been built in earnest -- correct instinct, applied one layer too early relative to proven need.\",\"Soft boundary inconsistent with stated posture: repository-capable context_paths are only prompt guidance, not an enforced sandbox, which is a real but currently accepted (ADR-038) risk given the trusted single-user framing.\"],\"gdd_iteration_concerns\":[\"Per-task conformance correctly treats a GDD hash change as invalidating that task's evidence (needs_revalidation), which is the right per-task reaction to a moving canon.\",\"There is no automated way to know, after a GDD edit, which of the 37 task contracts are affected without a full (expensive, human-gated) reconciliation run -- CURRENT_STATE.md itself acknowledges scoped impact analysis is only an intended future capability.\",\"Task contracts store literal quoted GDD passages as gdd_evidence/acceptance criteria; this creates a second, static copy of canon per task that can silently drift from the canonical GDD text with no diffing mechanism between Pipeline/GDDRAG chunks and the embedded task quotes.\",\"Because the GDD is explicitly expected to keep changing while the game is built, and because the project's own real experience already shows non-trivial correction churn (schema v1->v2, the 8/8 review finding on mutable status), the same category of drift risk plausibly exists for GDD-embedded task text and has not yet been exercised or tested against an actual GDD edit.\"],\"throughput_assessment\":\"Since Milestone 1 completed (2026-08-21), three straight implementation stages spanning the following two-day window (through 2026-08-23) produced zero additional lines of shipped gameplay code and zero tasks moved through the new pipeline end to end. All delivered work was either state/authority correction (a legitimate response to a real defect) or a dual-provider transport layer whose only production consumer is the architecture-review tool itself. The only game feature ever actually delivered (NSC-023, the isometric camera) was built through the older, now-orphaned Assignment 6 GER prototype, not through any of the infrastructure built in the last three stages. On current evidence, this pipeline has not yet demonstrated any throughput gain over a human developer working directly in Unity, and its write-incapable state means it structurally cannot demonstrate one until that gap is closed.\",\"human_intervention_points\":[\"Every GDD-derived design ambiguity must be resolved by a human before a task can be dispatched (explicitly blocking NSC-003 today: Input Action ownership, spell/movement/door arbitration, click vs. hold steering, destination/cancellation semantics, movement-restriction ownership).\",\"All Play Mode/runtime validation approval is manual (NSC-023's conformance record required 'explicit human Play Mode approval by Vincent Liguori').\",\"Artifact Authority Gate outcomes (AUTHORIZED/REJECTED/NEEDS_HUMAN_REVIEW) are conceptually human-adjacent decisions, though the gate itself is unimplemented.\",\"Every merge to main remains human-gated by design (ADR-006/ADR-007); no automatic merge exists or is proposed for the near term.\",\"Dispatch/readiness authorization is explicitly denied by policy (taskcontrol authorize returns DENIED) until a human approves a dispatch policy that does not yet exist.\",\"Any GDD edit currently requires a human to decide whether it is material enough to trigger full reconciliation, since no automated impact-scoping exists.\"],\"next_slice\":{\"title\":\"One real write-capable ticket, narrowly scoped, through the existing evidence/authority model -- not another provider or another review pass\",\"why\":\"The architecture's core promise (deterministic authority + bounded worker + evidence-gated completion) has never been exercised end to end because no provider can write, and the one proven repair loop (GER) is not wired into the new stack. Proving or falsifying real throughput leverage requires landing exactly one real ticket through write + validate + merge, not further generalizing the transport layer.\",\"deliverables\":[\"Human resolves the specific NSC-003 design ambiguities already listed in CURRENT_STATE.md (Input Action ownership, arbitration, click-vs-hold, cancellation, restriction ownership) -- a small, concrete, human-only decision, not new infrastructure.\",\"Extend exactly one provider adapter (Claude, since it is furthest along) with repository_write scoped only to NSC-003's already-declared exclusive_resources paths (InputSystem_Actions.inputactions, DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs, DoorPrototype.unity) rather than a generic write capability.\",\"Port the minimal Assignment 6 GER shape (generate -> deterministic/Unity evaluate -> runtime feedback -> refine -> circuit breaker) onto this one ticket through TaskExecutionRunner, reusing the existing evidence-record/conformance model for gating completion.\",\"Manual human branch/commit/merge (do not build supervisor or worktree automation for this slice) with fresh human diff review before merge.\",\"Record what actually broke or was missing while doing this, per the project's own stated development rule, before adding any further generalized infrastructure.\"],\"proof_of_value\":\"A merged NSC-003 commit whose completion is provable through the existing evidence-derived conformance model (a new BASE-NSC-003-<commit> record deriving 'conformant'), with the write path, GER loop, and human gates all exercised on one real feature -- the first genuine throughput data point this pipeline has produced since Milestone 1.\"},\"do_not_build_yet\":[\"Codex write capability or any Claude-vs-Codex comparison/dual-provider launcher -- no proven need yet and the existing single-provider path is not even write-capable.\",\"Progressive Decomposer and Artifact Authority Gate implementations -- NSC-003 is already decomposition_state: concrete; nothing currently blocked needs them.\",\"RAG-backed compact context builder / targeted context packs -- the project's own current-state notes say the GDD is small enough to hand over whole until top-k coverage is proven necessary.\",\"Supervisor loop, task claiming/leasing, branch/worktree automation, Draft PR automation, GitHub Issues/Projects sync, continuous autonomy, or parallel workers.\",\"Any further ArchitectureReview investment (a third provider, a comparison pipeline, additional reviewer roles) until at least one real ticket has shipped through the new pipeline.\",\"Generalizing repository_write beyond the one scoped ticket path until that narrow path is proven reliable.\"],\"alternative_architecture\":{\"needed\":false,\"description\":\"The existing skeleton -- deterministic authority for state/evidence/conformance, bounded replaceable LLM workers, human-gated write/merge, GDD as hash-bound canon -- does not need to be replaced. What is needed is enforcement of the project's own already-written priority rule (ADR-019/'Current Development Rule'): stop adding general-purpose transport/process infrastructure and land one real, narrowly-scoped, write-capable ticket through the existing model before building anything else.\",\"why_better\":\"Not applicable; no replacement architecture is being proposed. The fix is sequencing and scope discipline within the current design, not a structural redesign.\"},\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md\",\"observation\":\"Explicitly states no provider supports repository_write, approved_command_execution, or production ExecutionCrew orchestration, and that zero tasks are authorized for dispatch; also documents that all Stage 3/4 work since Milestone 1 targeted ArchitectureReview migration, not gameplay execution.\"},{\"path\":\"Tasks/NSC-003.yaml\",\"observation\":\"A concretely specified, GDD-grounded, dependency-free implementation task with defined exclusive_resources and completion gates -- ready in every sense except human design-ambiguity resolution and pipeline write capability, yet untouched since bootstrap.\"},{\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskExecution/task_runner.py\",\"observation\":\"39-line thin wrapper around AgentRunner; only exercised by a smoke test, never run against a real task.\"},{\"path\":\"Docs/AI-Pipeline/08_STAGE_4B_CLAUDE_CODE_PROVIDER.md\",\"observation\":\"Confirms the initial ClaudeCodeProvider rejects repository_read/search/write and any nonempty capability set at commit time; write capability is not even attempted yet.\"},{\"path\":\"Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md\",\"observation\":\"Documents the only feature (isometric camera) actually delivered, using a GER loop with runtime-feedback repair and no-op detection that has not been ported into the new AgentRuntime/TaskExecution stack.\"},{\"path\":\"Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/README.md\",\"observation\":\"Confirms ArchitectureReview now runs 8 reviewers x synthesis x adversarial critique through both Claude and Codex via generic AgentRuntime, with dual-provider comparison explicitly stated as unimplemented future work -- i.e., the dual-provider engineering has no near-term consumer.\"},{\"path\":\"Docs/AI-Pipeline/00_MASTER_CONTEXT.md\",\"observation\":\"States ADR-019 ('the pipeline must advance the game while it is being built') and 'From Milestone 2 onward, infrastructure should increasingly be proven by advancing actual No Safe Circle gameplay' -- a rule the last three implementation stages did not follow.\"},{\"path\":\"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/PlayerMovement.cs\",\"observation\":\"Existing WASD-only movement implementation confirms NSC-003's repository_evidence_at_bootstrap is accurate and the task is a real, bounded, non-speculative rewrite target.\"}],\"confidence\":0.78,\"biggest_uncertainty\":\"Whether the team's actual next move (beyond what CURRENT_STATE.md documents) is to pivot toward a write-capable single-ticket slice as recommended here, or to continue the pattern of general-purpose infrastructure (e.g., the Stage 4B doc's own forward pointer to a Stage 5 'ExecutionCrew role layer') before ever landing real game code -- that choice determines whether the sequencing flaw identified here gets corrected or repeats a third time.\"}","structured_output":{"architecture_summary":"The target design is sound in skeleton: a deterministic local authority (persistent task-contract graph, Git-committed evidence records, hash-bound GDD conformance derivation) owns 'what is true', while bounded LLM workers (currently Claude and OpenAI/Codex behind a shared AgentRuntime transport) act as replaceable, evidence-gated implementers with human merge/approval as the final gate. Schema-v2 task contracts correctly separate approved definition from mutable completion claims, and Phase 3's evidence-derived conformance state machine correctly ties completion to committed Git/GDD-hash facts rather than self-reported status. However, three consecutive implementation stages since Milestone 1 (Phase 1-3 state correction, then Stage 3-4A-4D AgentRuntime/provider-adapter work) have been spent entirely on process/meta-infrastructure. The concrete deliverable of all Stage 4 work is that ArchitectureReview -- a tool that reviews the pipeline itself -- now runs through a fully generalized, dual-provider (Claude + Codex), fail-closed transport layer with capability mapping, budget translation, and trust-boundary hardening. No provider adapter supports repository_write; TaskExecutionRunner is an untested 39-line wrapper never exercised on a real task; and the one demonstrated repair loop that actually shipped a working feature (Assignment 6 GER with runtime-feedback repair and no-op detection) has not been ported to the new AgentRuntime/TaskExecution stack at all. Meanwhile NSC-003, the team's own designated 'strong anchor' ready task, sits untouched, and CURRENT_STATE.md itself now says it needs further human design resolution before dispatch. The architecture's philosophy is correct; its recent build sequencing has repeatedly violated the project's own stated rule (ADR-019) that infrastructure must be exercised on real gameplay work rather than becoming a self-perpetuating side project.","overall_verdic