s validation input; no-op refinement counted as failed progress) are real lessons from an actual failure (the Assignment 6 camera) and were correctly generalized as durable project rules.","Deterministic scene builder + EditMode/PlayMode test pattern (DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder + CommittedSceneCameraConformanceTests) keeps Unity scene state reproducible and testable rather than hand-edited, which is good practice this project actually uses.","Restraint on supervisor, worktrees, GitHub dashboard, continuous autonomy, and parallel workers -- these remain correctly unimplemented rather than spawned speculatively, showing the team can defer some things well.","Fail-closed defaults for unsupported capabilities, non-null token_limit, and repository_write are conservative and appropriate for a trusted single-developer project that has not yet earned autonomous write trust."],"structural_flaws":["No provider adapter (Claude or Codex) supports repository_write or approved_command_execution; the entire Stage 4 investment therefore cannot commit a single line of game code today.","The one proven repair/quality loop (Assignment 6 GER: evaluate -> runtime feedback -> refine -> circuit breaker) has not been integrated into AgentRuntime/TaskExecution at all; if write capability were added tomorrow, the new pipeline would ship code with less quality gating than the prototype that already worked.","Task contracts embed literal quoted GDD text as gdd_evidence/acceptance criteria across 37 files with no automated mechanism to detect when a GDD edit has invalidated those embedded quotes short of a full, expensive, human-gated reconciliation run.","AgentInvocationRequest/TaskExecutionRequest separation (ADR-039) is architecturally defensible but was built for multiple hypothetical consumers (ExecutionCrew, Reconciliation) when it currently has exactly one real consumer (ArchitectureReview) that does not even need task identity -- premature generalization ahead of proven need.","Repository-capable context_paths are described as 'prompt guidance rather than a hardened sandbox boundary' -- the read containment is soft/trust-based, acceptable for a single trusted developer but inconsistent with the otherwise heavy fail-closed posture applied elsewhere."],"observed_failure_solutions":["Static-pass-but-runtime-broken camera (Assignment 6) -> runtime evidence made first-class validation input (ADR-015), proven to work.","Refiner claiming 'implemented' with no file changes (Assignment 6 Pass 3) -> no-op refinement now counts as failed repair against the circuit-breaker budget (ADR-016), proven to work.","Mutable task status files could self-declare completion without evidence -> task-contract schema 2.0 plus Phase 3 evidence-derived conformance removed status as an authority field and requires committed Git/GDD-hash-bound proof."],"hypothetical_failure_solutions":["Full dual-provider (Claude + Codex) capability-mapping, budget-translation, and fail-closed enforcement layer -- built for a provider swap or comparison that has never happened and is explicitly deferred future work.","Adversarial provider trust-boundary hardening (malformed/cyclic JSON, polymorphic mutable values, malicious provider output) in AgentRuntime -- defends against an adversarial model operator in a project ADR-038 itself frames as a trusted single-user boundary.","Multi-model independent verification crew for reconciliation bootstrap (2+ Claude models auditing coverage) -- used once successfully, but kept as standing infrastructure for 'later substantial reconciliation events' that have not recurred.","Generalized AgentInvocationRequest/TaskExecutionRequest layering above AgentRuntime to support future ExecutionCrew and Reconciliation consumers that do not yet exist."],"overengineering":["Running the full 8-reviewer + synthesis + adversarial-critique ArchitectureReview process through two independently engineered providers before either provider can write a single file is disproportionate to any near-term decision it enables.","Building generic, schema-validated, budget-enforced AgentRuntime capability plumbing (repository_read/search/write, approved_command_execution, token_limit, turn_limit translation) primarily to serve a self-review tool rather than the one real pending gameplay ticket.","Maintaining and documenting a standing multi-model verification-crew capability for reconciliation bootstrap when only one bootstrap event has ever required it."],"missing_components":["Any working write-capable execution path from AgentRuntime/TaskExecution through to a Git commit -- currently the single biggest gap for delivering any real feature.","A GER-equivalent evaluate/refine/circuit-breaker loop wired into the new AgentRuntime/TaskExecution stack (currently only exists, disconnected, in the Assignment 6 prototype).","A scoped GDD-change-impact mechanism that maps an edited GDD passage to the specific task contracts whose acceptance criteria/gdd_evidence quote it, short of full reconciliation.","Any implementation of the supervisor, branch/worktree/Draft-PR automation, RAG-backed compact context builder, Progressive Decomposer, or Artifact Authority Gate -- all remain design documents only, which is fine as long as they are not built before the write-capable single-ticket loop is proven."],"state_and_authority_concerns":["Necessary and currently correct: task-contract definition vs. immutable evidence record vs. derived current-conformance state are three distinct, non-overlapping authorities, each committed to Git, with no single source claiming to 'be' completion truth.","Necessary and currently correct: readiness/dispatch authorization is explicitly and verifiably denied (taskcontrol ready/authorize both fail closed), so no accidental autonomous execution can occur.","Duplicative/premature: the AgentInvocationRequest vs. TaskExecutionRequest split exists mainly to protect a provider-neutral layer from a task-execution consumer that has not yet 