was built through the older, now-orphaned Assignment 6 GER prototype, not through any of the infrastructure built in the last three stages. On current evidence, this pipeline has not yet demonstrated any throughput gain over a human developer working directly in Unity, and its write-incapable state means it structurally cannot demonstrate one until that gap is closed.","human_intervention_points":["Every GDD-derived design ambiguity must be resolved by a human before a task can be dispatched (explicitly blocking NSC-003 today: Input Action ownership, spell/movement/door arbitration, click vs. hold steering, destination/cancellation semantics, movement-restriction ownership).","All Play Mode/runtime validation approval is manual (NSC-023's conformance record required 'explicit human Play Mode approval by Vincent Liguori').","Artifact Authority Gate outcomes (AUTHORIZED/REJECTED/NEEDS_HUMAN_REVIEW) are conceptually human-adjacent decisions, though the gate itself is unimplemented.","Every merge to main remains human-gated by design (ADR-006/ADR-007); no automatic merge exists or is proposed for the near term.","Dispatch/readiness authorization is explicitly denied by policy (taskcontrol authorize returns DENIED) until a human approves a dispatch policy that does not yet exist.","Any GDD edit currently requires a human to decide whether it is material enough to trigger full reconciliation, since no automated impact-scoping exists."],"next_slice":{"title":"One real write-capable ticket, narrowly scoped, through the existing evidence/authority model -- not another provider or another review pass","why":"The architecture's core promise (deterministic authority + bounded worker + evidence-gated completion) has never been exercised end to end because no provider can write, and the one proven repair loop (GER) is not wired into the new stack. Proving or falsifying real throughput leverage requires landing exactly one real ticket through write + validate + merge, not further 